nes) — story orchestrator, references BIL_PRECI specifically (29 hits, 7 functions)\n- **Per-mission script mapping**: Each mission has 1-4 scripts referencing it. The primary gameplay script (highest hit count excluding the orchestrator) is identifiable per mission. Full mapping saved to `scratch/mission_to_decompiled_scripts.json`.\n\n### C. Joaat hash resolution working\n- Jenkins one-at-a-time (Joaat) hash function confirmed working — `joaat(\"story000\") = 0x5B5EEFFE` matches VmProgram, `joaat(\"finalchapterwindowtoss\") = 0x985E94E6` matches VmProgram\n- ALL mission IDs from mission_order.json can be hashed and matched against constants in decompiled code\n- Successfully resolved hashes in `func_10AA55` of orchestrator:\n  - 0xF8FB7ACC = BIL_FINALE_M (Ending M/Mendez)\n  - 0x96F9A142 = BIL_FINAL_B (Ending B/Brian)\n  - 0x2625203A = MNY_HOTEL\n  - 0x32367ABD = MNY_HOTEL_AUTOLAUNCH\n  - 0x3C9B93B4 = MTL_WAKE\n  - 0x9530AB91 = FIN_CONT\n  - 0xE48C934A = FT_KMODSHP_SECOND\n  - And more (see work accomplished list)\n\n### D. Named script files catalogued (58 total)\nKey named scripts: `story000.ysc.cs`, `shared.ysc.cs` (204MB — DO NOT bulk-read), `finalchapterwindowtoss.ysc.cs`, `finalecredits.ysc.cs`, `introcredits.ysc.cs`, `robbergetawaydriverprep.ysc.cs`, `realestate.ysc.cs`, `smashandgrab.ysc.cs`, `escapetime.ysc.cs`, plus compound scripts for factions (Kingfishers, Kolt, Guardia Brothers, La Polilla Negra, San4San, M7, PTTY, Final Chapter, Criminal enterprises)\n\n### E. Previous flowcharts generated (accuracy disputed)\n- PNGs created for all 5 chapters + combined + speedrun versions\n- Markdown artifact `gta6_mission_flow_chart.md` exists\n- User and community flagged accuracy issues — these need regeneration once real dependency data is extracted\n\n### F. `notes_facts.py` from work directory run successfully\n- Confirmed mission variant entries (e.g., BIL_PICK has DAY/NIGHT variants, BIL_MOTEL has VIOLENT/NON_VIOLENT, BIL_PENT has M_MENDEZ/B_BRIAN endings, AIR_CATER has DHF/DHP/DHS data hack variants, AIR_FINAL has DATA_HACK_FAILED/PASSED)\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n\n### Architecture of decompiled scripts\n- Scripts are RAGE YSC bytecode transpiled to C# under `namespace Americas.Decompiled` using `Rage.ScriptDecompiler.GTA6.Runtime` targeting .NET 8.0\n- Each script has a `[VmProgram(0xHASH)]` attribute — the hash is the Joaat of the original script name\n- Functions are `[VmFunction(0xOFFSET)]` — named `func_XXXXXX`\n- String literals are stripped — mission IDs, item names, etc. are stored as 32-bit Joaat hashes in `store_i32` calls\n- Mission state checks use `Virtual.type_37658EE3464E5234.Method_1(context, hash, flag)` — this appears to be a \"is mission completed/active?\" check\n- Mission state sets use `Virtual.type_37658EE3464E5234.Method_0(context, hash, flag)` — this appears to be a \"mark mission state\" call\n\n### Critical file: `0xD2601E252151E04B.ysc.cs` — The Master Mission Orchestrator\n- VmProgram 0x0E8E47D1\n- ~1.56M lines (massive file)\n- Contains the central mission dispatch logic across 20 functions\n- `func_109E09` (193 hits) — largest function, references almost every mission. This is likely the main state machine transition table.\n- `func_12EB6F` (42 hits) — references MTL_CONT, ANT_CHASE, ROB_VEH, AIR_TAIL, ROB_BOAT_J_JASON\n- `func_24BCE4` (31 hits) — references MTL_MUD, MTL_CONT, BIL_MOTEL variants, BAN_SETUP, BAN_FINAL, CLB_VIDEO\n- `func_10AA55` (24 hits) — Chapter transitions: handles FIN_CONT, BIL_FINALE_M, BIL_FINAL_B, MNY_HOTEL, MTL_WAKE, FT_KMODSHP_SECOND — this is likely the chapter boundary handler\n- Lines 572900-573094: `func_10AA55` contains a switch-case on mission ID hashes. When local_0 matches BIL_FINALE_M or BIL_FINAL_B, it jumps to label_10ACD8 which calls `Native._0x58BECE7D02A750A7` (possibly a cutscene/credits trigger). When it matches MNY_HOTEL or MNY_HOTEL_AUTOLAUNCH, it jumps to label_10AC0A which sets multiple mission flags.\n\n### Key JSON data files in Xbox build\n- `output/mission_order.json` — Master document with missions, chapters, replay_menu_cross_mission_links, cmissions_entries_not_in_replay_menu. Dict with keys: metadata, missions (97), replay_menu_cross_mission_links (4), cmissions_entries_not_in_replay_menu (50)\n- `work/cmissions.json` — Raw CMissions table from common.rpf XML\n- `work/cmissions.xml` — XML version\n- `work/progress_missions.json` — Progress UI dataset (uiProgressDataset from data.rpf RBF0)\n- `work/decomp_mission_refs.json` — Maps 199 decompiled script filenames to {function: [[line, mission_id]]} — THE KEY INDEX for finding which scripts handle which missions\n- `work/decomp_survey.json`, `work/pso_survey.json`, `work/hash_probe.json` — Additional analysis data\n- `work/rbf_progress_dataset.json` — UI progress dataset\n\n### Existing analysis scripts in `work/` directory\nThe Xbox build's `work/` directory contains pre-built Python analysis scripts (created by whoever prepared the build):\n- `decomp_mission_refs.py` — Builds the decomp_mission_refs.json index\n- `decomp_refs_report.py` — Reports per-function mission references for a given script\n- `notes_facts.py` — Prints facts from mission_order.json\n- `hash_probe.py`, `mission_hash_table.py` — Hash resolution tools\n- `build_outputs.py`, `validate_outputs.py` — Build/validate the mission_order.json\n- `progress_missions.py`, `progress_explore.py` — Parse progress UI data\n\n### Failures and constraints\n- **shared.ysc.cs is 204MB** — bulk reading or regex scanning causes task hangs. Always use targeted `grep_search` or line-by-line streaming.\n- **PowerShell inline regex escaping** — Python one-liners with regex in PowerShell break due to bracket escaping. Always write to a `.py` file and execute.\n- **String extraction yielded zero game strings** — The decompiled scripts contain NO readable string literals for mission names/dialogue. All strings were compiled to Joaat hashes. The only way to resolve them is hash matching against known mission IDs.\n- **Direct VmProgram matching failed** — Only 1 of 97 missions (`robbergetawaydriverprep`) has a filename matching its mission ID. The hash-named scripts cannot be identified by filename alone; they must be identified through the `decomp_mission_refs.json` cross-reference.\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited/Created Files\n- `scratch/analyze_story_scripts.py` — Extracts strings and native calls from story000.ysc.cs\n- `scratch/scan_all_script_strings.py` — Scans all 745 scripts (excluding shared) for string literals\n- `scratch/decompiled_script_strings.txt` — 24,596 unique strings found (almost all decompiler primitives)\n- `scratch/print_mission_order.py` — Pretty-prints mission_order.json by chapter\n- `scratch/match_mission_scripts.py` — Attempts to match mission IDs to VmProgram hashes (only 1 direct match found)\n- `scratch/map_decompiled_to_missions.py` — Maps all 199 script files to their mission references using decomp_mission_refs.json\n- `scratch/mission_to_decompiled_scripts.json` — JSON output of mission→script mapping\n- All scratch files are in `C:\\Users\\<user>\\.gemini\\antigravity-cli\\brain\\96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c\\scratch\\`\n\n### Viewed Files (Key Sections)\n- **`C:\\Users\\<user>\\Downloads\\americas_scripts_23_11_2026\\0xD2601E252151E04B.ysc.cs`** (Master orchestrator, ~1.56M lines)\n  - Lines 1-50: Header, imports, VmProgram(0x0E8E47D1), basic functions\n  - Lines 572900-573094: `func_10AA55` — Chapter transition handler with switch on mission ID hashes. Contains the BIL_FINALE_M/BIL_FINAL_B ending logic and MTL_WAKE/MNY_HOTEL chapter starts. THIS IS THE KEY FUNCTION for understanding chapter boundaries.\n  - Lines 573096-573133: `func_10AD05` — Checks BIL_FINALE_M and BIL_FINAL_B completion flags (the two finale ending variants)\n  - **NOT YET READ**: `func_109E09` (193 hits, the main state machine — likely starts around line ~570K based on function ordering), `func_12EB6F` (42 hits), `func_24BCE4` (31 hits)\n\n- **`C:\\Users\\<user>\\Downloads\\americas_scripts_23_11_2026\\story000.ysc.cs`** (6.28MB, ~127K lines)\n  - Lines 1-100: Header, VmProgram(0x5B5EEFFE), 7 imports, basic entry point functions\n  - References BIL_PRECI specifically (29 hits across 7 functions) — needs deeper investigation\n\n- **`C:\\Users\\<user>\\Downloads\\americas_scripts_23_11_2026\\finalchapterwindowtoss.ysc.cs`** (35,462 lines)\n  - Lines 1-150: Header, VmProgram(0x985E94E6), stub functions\n  - Lines 217-798: Heavy Native calls (unnamed hashes like 0x35AC71F2B30D834B, 0xF2BC1ABE7FE3E12A)\n\n- **`C:\\Users\\<user>\\Downloads\\GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK\\output\\mission_order.json`** — Full mission catalog (described in detail above)\n- **`C:\\Users\\<user>\\Downloads\\GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK\\work\\decomp_mission_refs.json`** — 199-entry index mapping scripts to mission references\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n### What was being worked on\nThe user said: \"go ahead and coniture revrese engineering the mission order, do not houklsationte or use sources outside the game files, if something is not possibele, tell me\"\n\nWe were actively tracing the mission state machine in the master orchestrator `0xD2601E252151E04B.ysc.cs` to extract the **mission prerequisite/dependency graph**. We confirmed that:\n1. Mission IDs are stored as Joaat hashes\n2. `Virtual.type_37658EE3464E5234.Method_1()` checks if a mission is complete\n3. `Virtual.type_37658EE3464E5234.Method_0()` sets a mission flag\n4. The orchestrator function `func_10AA55` handles chapter transitions\n\n### Exact next steps\n1. **Write a comprehensive hash resolver script** that:\n   - Takes `0xD2601E252151E04B.ysc.cs` as input\n   - Finds ALL `store_i32(..., 0x0, HASH)` patterns followed by `Method_0` or `Method_1` calls\n   - Resolves each hash against the known mission ID Joaat table\n   - Outputs the dependency graph: \"when mission X is checked (Method_1), mission Y is set (Method_0)\"\n\n2. **Focus on `func_109E09`** (193 hits, the largest) — this is the main state transition table. Find its starting line in `0xD2601E252151E04B.ysc.cs` by searching for `[VmFunction(0x109E09)]` and read the full function to map all mission transitions.\n\n3. **Also analyze `func_12EB6F`** (42 hits) and **`func_24BCE4`** (31 hits) for additional dependency edges.\n\n4. **For each mission**, identify which missions must be completed before it becomes available, using the Method_1 (check) → Method_0 (set) pattern.\n\n5. **Regenerate flowcharts** once the full dependency graph is extracted, replacing the inaccurate previous versions.\n\n### Skill files read\n- `C:\\Users\\<user>\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\reverse-engineer-anything\\SKILL.md` — Read in prior session for REA methodology. The next agent should re-read this if using REA MCP tools.\n\n### Key tool available\n- The `work/decomp_refs_report.py` script in the Xbox build can be used to get per-function mission reference summaries: `python work/decomp_refs_report.py work/decomp_mission_refs.json \"0xD2601E252151E04B.ysc.cs\"`\n\nYou have the 47 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1795562572299]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/<user>/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c/.tempmediaStorage/media_1795562572299.png\nLast Edited: 2026-11-24T23:22:52Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1795562577913]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/<user>/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c/.tempmediaStorage/media_1795562577913.png\nLast Edited: 2026-11-24T23:22:57Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1795562582348]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/<user>/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c/.tempmediaStorage/media_1795562582348.png\nLast Edited: 2026-11-24T23:23:02Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1795562587887]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/<user>/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c/.tempmediaStorage/media_1795562587887.png\nLast Edited: 2026-11-24T23:23:07Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media